understand both normative, how does the developing brain learn in an ideal case in a healthy way, also when things go awry in development, either early on or later, how does that impact knowledge and skills, language delays, and so on. If we had a better understanding of the underlying brain systems that absorb our experiences and build memories, that might point to some potential ways of either diagnosing or treating developmental disorders in the long run. So what's next? I mean, are you continuing the same line of research? Are you expanding, moving into other areas? The study that I referenced before, which was published in science in March, is a starting point. This is showing that infants have the capacity.

