to form episodic memories in the hippocampus beginning around one year of age. Because we were doing both the encoding and the retrieval in the same study, it was only a few minutes before they were tested on their memory. So we know that they can store a memory, but we don't know how long it lasts. And this is a really critical question when we think about our lack of early memories. We're really talking years. It's our autobiography. And so it's an open question about how durable these early memories.

